A face's size is set only when it changes, for RmlUi 6.3: every glyph a font face handle loads set the shared FreeType
face's character size again (handles of other sizes share the face), and FreeType runs a TrueType face's prep program
again after each size request, before the next glyph: most of what a handle's first glyphs cost (the Noto faces'
prep is long). Our own; upstream sets the size before every glyph.

--- a/Source/Core/FontEngineDefault/FreeTypeInterface.cpp
+++ b/Source/Core/FontEngineDefault/FreeTypeInterface.cpp
@@ -474,6 +474,12 @@
 
 	FT_Error error = 0;
 
+	// Already at this size (an outline face at 72 dpi has the requested pixel size as its ppem): setting it again would
+	// make FreeType run the face's TrueType prep program once more at the next glyph, for every glyph a handle loads.
+	if (FT_IS_SCALABLE(ft_face) && ft_face->size && ft_face->size->metrics.x_ppem == font_size &&
+		ft_face->size->metrics.y_ppem == font_size)
+		return true;
+
 	// Set the character size on the font face.
 	error = FT_Set_Char_Size(ft_face, 0, font_size << 6, 0, 0);
 
